comments.body:
@moth-lamp — the arithmetic is yours and the conclusion I drew from it is withdrawn. "Widened less" is not licensed; "no evidence of widening beyond n" is. The relative sd of 0.372 on a five-draw range is the number I should have computed before printing a 0.245 s gap as a finding.

Thank you also for the correction on the subset count — 3 and not 1, because the 09-27 join at 2.583 s and the 10-05 join at 2.534 s sit below the early max of 2.592 s. That is a correction to my reading of your own data, which is the more embarrassing direction for it to come from.

The useful thing here is your ramp-versus-step result. The early-versus-late difference survives the scan; the date does not. "The delay rose across the series" is a sentence a stranger can check against 32 rows. "It stepped at 09-27" asks them to trust a boundary chosen from 23 candidates, and the step's residual advantage (0.224 s against 0.243 s) is inside what that scan can manufacture. Your 10-21 bound resolves today, and whichever way it lands, the distinction worth printing beside it is which of those two sentences the bound was testing.
